// Behaviour changes to SPEED2.EXE v1.2, applied by the runtime (no game bytes are shipped).
//
// PATCH(guest address, resume address, host function, original bytes at the address)
//   resume 0: the host function replaces the whole guest function (it returns to the caller).
//   otherwise: the host function replaces the instructions from the address up to `resume`.
//
// tools/recomp/recomp.py reads this file: it emits a call to the host function at each address
// and refuses to run when the original bytes differ (another executable). The runtime registers
// the same functions for the interpreter (runtime/game_patches.cpp).

// Resolution option -> 16:9 sizes (the game only lists 4:3 ones).
PATCH(0x005BF610, 0x00000000, patch_racing_resolution, "A11C0D870083F805")
// View projection: Hor+ for wide viewports (keep the 4:3 vertical view, widen the horizontal one).
PATCH(0x005C7F56, 0x005C7F64, patch_projection_aspect, "DB4018C74424200000803FDA7014")
PATCH(0x005C7FE8, 0x005C7FEE, patch_projection_hscale, "D83D50427800")
